WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.436
-President Trump has been
floating the possibility

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.972
of using military force
in Venezuela.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.174
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:11.944
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:14.747
You might recall that during
the presidential campaign,

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.483
Trump tried to pretend
that he was anti-war.

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.619
Despite supporting the Iraq war
at the time,

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.854
he claimed repeatedly
that he was against it

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:24.690
and even confronted Jeb Bush
to his face

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.226
about his brother's decision
to invade Iraq.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:32.465
-Obviously, the war in Iraq was
a big fat mistake, all right?

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:36.235
The war in Iraq, we spent
$2 trillion, thousands of lives.

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:37.536
We don't even have it.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.105
Iran is taking over Iraq

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.641
with the second-largest
oil reserves in the world.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.443
Obviously, it was a mistake.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.712
George Bush made a mistake.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.180
We can make mistakes.
But that one was a beauty.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.249
We should have never
been in Iraq.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.551
We have destabilized
the Middle East.

00:00:52.551 --> 00:00:55.421
-"And if I'm president,
I won't stop at the Middle East.

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.457
I'll destabilize
the entire world."

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.724
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:02.495
Also, I don't know
why you're yelling at Jeb

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.730
about the Iraq war.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.632
You think they checked with him?

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.799
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.702
They barely let him
in the family photos.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.638
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:16.142
Look how red Trump's face is.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.244
How is it possible
for a human being

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:21.014
to blend into their background
like that?

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.948
I knew he changed positions
all the time.

00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:26.285
But I didn't think
he was an actual chameleon.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:29.055
Comments like that led some
pundits to the absurd conclusion

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:32.058
that Trump was somehow anti-war,
like this now infamous headline

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.060
from the "New York Times"
op-ed page --

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.928
"Donald the Dove,
Hillary the Hawk."

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:39.665
Donald Trump is many things,
but he is not a dove.

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:42.835
New Yorkers hate him,
and he eats fast food.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.737
He's clearly a pigeon.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.372
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.574
He even --
[ Applause ]

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.911
For what it's worth...

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.781
he even stands like a pigeon.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.884
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.986
And we knew --
we knew Trump was lying

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.021
about his supposed
anti-war leanings

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.390
because he kept repeating one of
his favorite talking points --

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.493
"When we invaded Iraq, we should
have taken the country's oil."

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:10.163
He even foreshadowed
a possible return to Iraq

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:13.632
in a speech at CIA headquarters
the day after his inauguration.

00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:16.635
-The old expression -- "To
the victor belong the spoils."

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:19.238
You remember I always used to
say, "Keep the oil."

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:22.541
I wasn't a fan of Iraq.
I didn't want to go into Iraq.

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:26.579
But I will tell you, when
we were in, we got out wrong.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:29.082
And I always said, in addition
to that, "Keep the oil."

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.084
Now, I said it
for economic reasons.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:33.019
But if you think about it, Mike,
if we kept the oil,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.520
you probably wouldn't have ISIS,

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.455
'cause that's where they made
their money in the first place.

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:40.325
So we should have kept the oil,
but okay.

00:02:40.325 --> 00:02:41.995
Maybe you'll have
another chance.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.328
-Wait, what?

00:02:43.328 --> 00:02:45.632
What do you mean,
another chance?

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.768
You can't just tease something
like that and then move on.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.603
That's like dropping news
on your parents

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.271
while you're hanging up
on the phone.

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:54.039
"Okay, Mom, I've got to run.
I love you, too.

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:56.742
Deb and I are splitting up.
Bye."

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.377
One of these days
we're going to find out

00:02:58.377 --> 00:02:59.846
that Trump sold the country
to Russia

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.314
in the middle
of one of his rambles.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.782
"We're having
the Clemson team over.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.717
We're serving them Big Macs.
They have that sauce.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:05.785
It's like Russian dressing,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.186
which, you know,
it's from Russia,

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:11.224
which is fitting because
they own the White House now."

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.658
And Iraq is not the only country

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.860
Trump has teased as a target
for regime change.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.528
According to
Bob Woodward's book "Fear,"

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:19.231
Trump once told former
Defense Secretary James Mattis

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:22.134
he wanted to take out
Syrian dictator Bashar al-Assad,

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:23.602
but Mattis ignored him.

00:03:23.602 --> 00:03:24.837
Trump called Mattis

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.706
and said he wanted
to assassinate the dictator.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.674
"Let's [bleep] kill him.
Let's go in.

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:30.909
Let's kill the [bleep] lot
of them," Trump said.

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:33.713
Mattis told the President
that he would get right on it,

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.482
but after hanging up the phone,
he told a senior aide,

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.284
"We're not gonna
do any of that."

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:41.654
It is amazing that
you can just ignore

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.723
the President
of the United States,

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.559
and he'll probably forget
what he asked you to do.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.028
He's like a dog who really wants
a tennis ball.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.797
If you just fake throw it
and then put it in a drawer,

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:53.499
he'll forget about it.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:56.435
So, Trump the dove asked
the Secretary of Defense

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:58.037
to kill a Syrian dictator

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:01.140
and teased a potential return to
Iraq to take the country's oil.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.276
And now he's threatening
the possibility

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.977
of military action in Venezuela.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.046
-We have now heard that
the Trump administration

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:11.084
has unveiled sanctions
on Venezuela's oil industry,

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.318
and they've actually implied

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.153
we could soon see
military action there.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.322
-Republican senator
Lindsey Graham confirmed

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.823
that President Trump has mused

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:20.326
about possible military
intervention in Venezuela.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.661
-Is there any circumstance

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.096
under which American forces
would get involved?

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:28.367
-Look, the President has made it
very clear on this matter

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.703
that all options
are on the table.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:33.806
-Are you considering
a military option for Venezuela?

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.140
-We're not considering anything,

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.642
but all options
are on the table.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.544
-Does that mean
you're considering...

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:42.081
-Just all options always.
All options are on the table.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.449
-All options are on the table.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.084
That's reminding me
of something.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.352
Oh, right.
There it is.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.753
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:49.255
"Help yourself, guys.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:53.259
All options are on the table.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:56.295
We have all
the McNugget sauces."

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:58.097
When Trump says all options
are on the table,

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.966
it's because he doesn't know
what the options are.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:01.767
He knows military,
and that's it.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:04.036
Someone should dare him
to name a second option.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:06.271
"Well, there's military,
then there's Army,

00:05:06.271 --> 00:05:09.575
and then if we have to,
we'll send in the space force."

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.043
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:13.345
Now, there's no question that
there's a serious humanitarian

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:14.814
and political crisis
in Venezuela,

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.716
and the regime
of President Nicolás Maduro,

00:05:17.716 --> 00:05:21.053
who won a rigged election
in May, is genuinely awful.

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:22.454
This is Maduro.

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:24.891
You probably recognize him
from the classic dictator look

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:26.959
sported by guys
like Joseph Stalin,

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.895
Saddam Hussein,
and the Soup Nazi.

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:30.162
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:31.330
Maduro has presided

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.132
over an economic catastrophe
in Venezuela.

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:35.501
Just to give you an idea,
Venezuela used to be

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.104
one of the world's richest
oil-producing countries.

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:42.107
Now there are widespread food
shortages and hyperinflation

00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:44.443
that has rendered the currency
essentially worthless.

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:47.480
-The economic free fall
is from falling oil prices

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.214
and failed economic policies.

00:05:49.214 --> 00:05:50.717
The government
printed more money,

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:53.920
and bills became so worthless,
women turned them into art.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.755
Inflation could hit 10,000,000%.

00:05:56.755 --> 00:05:59.491
That's how many bolívars
it costs to buy a chicken.

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:01.627
It takes a stack
of almost-worthless paper

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:02.995
to buy toilet paper.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.296
-Look at that.

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:06.132
That's how much money it takes
to buy toilet paper.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:09.902
You might as well use the money
instead of the toilet paper.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.105
"Honey, that Chipotle
isn't sitting well with me.

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:14.807
Can you pass me $1 million?"

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:17.609
Maduro has jailed prisoners,
cracked down on dissidents

00:06:17.609 --> 00:06:18.710
to try to stay in power.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.779
Meanwhile, many Western nations

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:23.983
have recognized
opposition leader Juan Guaidó

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:25.584
as the legitimate president,

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:28.121
which means there are
two rival presidents.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:30.189
The political situation
is so crazy,

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.191
there's even
a rival supreme court.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.126
And it isn't even in Venezuela.

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:37.029
For the last year and a half, a
second Venezuelan supreme court

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.931
has presided over
the country's laws

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.999
through the miracle
of cloud computing.

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:44.069
Its 33 jurists live in the U.S.,
Panama, Colombia, and Chile.

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:47.139
Every 15 days, they hold court
via video conference

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:49.742
in what Bloomberg called
"a Skype judiciary."

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:52.377
They're making supreme court
decisions via Skype.

00:06:52.377 --> 00:06:55.415
I can't even figure out
how to Skype with my mom.

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:57.316
Everything's on
a five-second delay,

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:58.818
and every other word cuts out.

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:01.020
That must be why
all their cases are called

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.189
"say that again" v.
"just send me a text."

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:06.025
There's no question
that Venezuela is in crisis.

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:09.362
The question is, what's the best
way to resolve the crisis

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.663
without making things worse?

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:13.099
On the one hand, countries
like Mexico and Uruguay

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:14.900
have already proposed
a new process

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.869
of inclusive
and credible negotiations

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:19.271
to seek a peaceful resolution
to the conflict.

00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:21.340
On the other hand,
the Trump administration

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.443
has chosen to back Guaidó
and impose sanctions.

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:27.546
Vice President Mike Pence
even secretly called Guaidó

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:28.647
and told him the U.S.

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:30.716
would support his claim
to the presidency

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.785
and recorded a message
to the Venezuelans

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:34.487
urging them to do the same.

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:35.954
-Hola.

00:07:35.954 --> 00:07:39.892
I'm Mike Pence, the Vice
President of the United States.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:42.861
The United States supports
the courageous decision

00:07:42.861 --> 00:07:47.366
by Juan Guaidó, the president
of your National Assembly,

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:50.569
to assert that body's
constitutional powers,

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:52.838
declare Maduro a usurper,

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:56.175
and call for the establishment
of a transitional government.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:08:00.145
We say to all the good people
of Venezuela,

00:08:00.145 --> 00:08:03.649
estamos con ustedes.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:04.950
We are with you.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.418
Muchas gracias.

00:08:06.418 --> 00:08:09.622
Y vayan con Dios.

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:10.823
-Wow.

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:13.358
Mike Pence's Spanish
makes Michael Bloomberg

00:08:13.358 --> 00:08:15.494
sound like the mayor
of Barcelona.

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:17.162
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.162 --> 00:08:18.730
There's something very odd

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:21.500
about hearing Mike Pence
say the word "hola."

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:25.037
It's like when the gym teacher
has to cover Spanish class.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:27.506
"Hola. Señor Perez
is out with strep.

00:08:27.506 --> 00:08:31.043
The assignment is on el boardo."

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:32.711
And while Pence
was backing Guaidó,

00:08:32.711 --> 00:08:34.780
Trump was apparently
floating the possibility

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.615
of military intervention
to Republicans

00:08:36.615 --> 00:08:38.617
like South Carolina senator
Lindsey Graham.

00:08:38.617 --> 00:08:42.154
And even Graham, one of the most
pro-war politicians in Congress,

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:43.889
told Trump that was a bad idea.

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:45.324
-Senator Lindsey Graham says

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:47.426
that recently
as a couple of weeks ago,

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.595
President Trump
discussed the possibility

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:51.597
of using military force
in Venezuela.

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:53.966
Graham, recalling
his conversation with Trump,

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:55.635
told Axios, "Trump said,

00:08:55.635 --> 00:08:58.403
'What do you think about
using military force?'

00:08:58.403 --> 00:09:01.173
And I said, 'Well,
you need to go slow on that.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:02.774
That could be problematic.'

00:09:02.774 --> 00:09:05.043
And he said,
'Well, I'm surprised.

00:09:05.043 --> 00:09:06.946
You want to invade everybody.'"

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:09.248
-Yeah, dude, seriously,
take a hint.

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:11.450
Even the guy who wants
to invade everybody

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.685
is telling you to relax.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:14.320
It's like Kathie Lee and Hoda

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.455
telling you to cool it
on the Pinot.

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:18.023
Now, the scary thing about Trump

00:09:18.023 --> 00:09:19.992
floating military action
in Venezuela

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:22.828
is that the people who used to
ignore his crazy fantasies,

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:24.630
like Mattis,
are no longer there.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.432
Now Trump is surrounded
by hard-liners

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:28.400
like National Security Advisor
John Bolton,

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.803
who's called for regime change
in several countries,

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:33.305
and then there's Treasury
Secretary Steve Mnuchin.

00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:35.440
On Monday, they held a briefing
at the White House

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.311
to unveil new sanctions
on Venezuela's oil sector.

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.345
-Today Treasury took action

00:09:40.345 --> 00:09:44.116
against Venezuela's
state-owned oil company PDVSA.

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:47.386
Persons operating
in the Venezuelan oil sector

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:50.222
may now be subject to sanctions.

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:53.592
Refineries in the United States
have already been taking steps

00:09:53.592 --> 00:09:56.829
to reduce the reliance
on imports from Venezuela.

00:09:56.829 --> 00:10:00.800
Those imports have fallen
substantially in recent months.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:03.702
-I'm sorry, but what is going on
with this map?

00:10:03.702 --> 00:10:06.305
It's not exactly a good look
for this White House

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:07.873
when the map has all of Russia

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:10.375
and only half
of the United States.

00:10:10.375 --> 00:10:11.810
Was this Trump's idea?

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.346
"This is the official map now.
California is gone."

00:10:14.346 --> 00:10:15.681
[ Laughter ]

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:17.282
Now, there's concern
among experts

00:10:17.282 --> 00:10:18.718
and some Democrats in Congress

00:10:18.718 --> 00:10:21.053
that the sanctions could only
make the economic situation

00:10:21.053 --> 00:10:23.055
in Venezuela worse
for the ordinary citizens.

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:25.223
But that wasn't the scariest
thing about the briefing.

00:10:25.223 --> 00:10:27.126
The scariest thing
was what they didn't say --

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:29.261
specifically, what Bolton had
on his notepad

00:10:29.261 --> 00:10:30.730
that was caught by the cameras.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.032
-"The Washington Post"
reports a notepad

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:35.534
held by National Security
Advisor John Bolton

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:37.736
appeared to disclose
a possible plan

00:10:37.736 --> 00:10:40.005
to send 5,000 U.S. troops
to Colombia.

00:10:40.005 --> 00:10:43.509
It comes amid rising tensions
between the U.S. and Venezuela.

00:10:43.509 --> 00:10:45.844
Bolton held the notepad
facing outward

00:10:45.844 --> 00:10:48.314
during a White House briefing
yesterday.

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:50.249
There were two items
scrawled on the pad --

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:54.653
"Afghanistan, welcome the talks"
and "5,000 troops to Colombia."

00:10:54.653 --> 00:10:55.954
-That's right.

00:10:55.954 --> 00:10:58.223
Bolton was holding his notepad
toward the cameras,

00:10:58.223 --> 00:11:01.093
and when they zoomed in, it said
"5,000 troops to Colombia."

00:11:01.093 --> 00:11:02.094
Here's my question.

00:11:02.094 --> 00:11:03.495
Why is he carrying around
a notepad

00:11:03.495 --> 00:11:05.797
with only two sentences on it?

00:11:05.797 --> 00:11:07.399
Just remember it.

00:11:07.399 --> 00:11:09.034
When I go to the bathroom,

00:11:09.034 --> 00:11:12.237
I don't need to write down
"brush teeth and floss."

00:11:12.237 --> 00:11:13.839
The bottom line is this.

00:11:13.839 --> 00:11:16.809
You can think Maduro is awful
and oppose him

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:19.412
and also think military action
is a bad idea.

00:11:19.412 --> 00:11:21.213
Those aren't mutually exclusive.

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:23.449
We probably shouldn't
trust the same guys

00:11:23.449 --> 00:11:25.551
who supported a disastrous war
in Iraq

00:11:25.551 --> 00:11:27.186
to do a better job in Venezuela.

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:29.588
Instead of threatening war,
maybe call up allies

00:11:29.588 --> 00:11:31.590
and countries in the region
and say...

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:32.657
-Hola.

00:11:32.657 --> 00:11:34.460
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.429
[ Cheers and applause ]

